error[ffi_parameter_type]: `o` of `count_plain` is declared `counted_by`, and the header's `struct opaque *` points at `struct opaque`, which it leaves incomplete — C counts in a type only C can size, so no count can be held to what is lent
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-395-a-count-in-a-type-the-header-hides-is-refused.hero:16:26
     |
  16 |     function count_plain(o: ptr counted_by n lent, n: u64) -> i64  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |                          ^
  note: §4.19: a counted parameter is lent the program's own bytes, a field or a record, and C counts them in what its pointer points at; where the header keeps that type opaque, declare `o` without `counted_by` and hand it a pointer C gave you

